      "properties": {
        "Node name for S&R": "MarkdownNote"
      },
      "widgets_values": [
        "# Stage 2 of 2 \u2014 assemble the cards\n\nReads the art stage 1 wrote and turns it into finished cards. **No API calls at all**, so\nevery run here is free and instant. Iterate on the border and the lettering as long as you like.\n\n## The handoff, received\n\n- **The deck definition** comes from `tarot/deck.json`, written by stage 1. Do not retype the\n  deck here \u2014 loading the same file is what guarantees the two stages agree about names, order\n  and scope. Rename a card in stage 1 and this stage letters the new name without being told.\n- **The art** comes from `tarot/derived-art/`. Stage 1 named it `00_the-fool.png`, which the\n  Slot Loader matches by slug *and* by index prefix, so it maps back onto the right positions\n  either way. Check its report anyway.\n\n## What you can do here for free\n\n`border` off gives full-bleed at the same trim size \u2014 the same run, both ways, by toggling one\nwidget. Add a second **Card Frame** node off the same input to get bordered and unbordered in\none pass.\n\n**Set `font_path`.** Pillow's built-in face is fine for placing the block and not fine for print.\n\n## Coming back later\n\nThis stage needs nothing but the two folders. A deck generated months ago re-assembles from\nits files with no cascade, no keys and no cost \u2014 which is the point of the split."
      ],
      "title": "Read me \u2014 stage 2 assembles",
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653"
    },
